   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Investing for impact against tuberculosis - Gabon (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gabon, Tuberculosis, Ministry of Health of the Gabonese Republic (MoH)This program has the following goals: By 2018, contribute to reducing TB morbidity and mortality among the Gabonese population. The objectives of this program are: Improve management and coordination capacity of NTP staff at all levels of health pyramid, including the capacity to ensure a good quality M&amp;E.  Improve the number of TB cases notification all forms (new cases and relapse) from 5 608 in 2014 to 9 144 cas in 2018 in the general population inlcuding the key populations.  Increase the treatment success rate in new TB cases bacteriologically confirmed from 57% to 85 % thanks to improvement in quality monitoring and care to patients on treatment.  Provide diagnostic to at least 10 % of MDR-TB expected cases and treat 100% of confirmed cases.  Provide HIV testing and counselling at the initiative of the service providers to at least 90% of TB patients and provide ARV and cotrimoxazole to at least  90%  of co-infected TB/HIV patients</narrative>
  </description>
